# plain-debris: from the menu, load the saved game setup/plain-debris writes (a new character
# with a scroll of Light of quality 1 in the pack's first slot, facing a wooden wall); drag the
# scroll out of the pack with the right button into the view, which throws it at the wall and
# breaks it; look down twice and at the pile of debris it leaves; drag the debris into the
# pack's first slot with the right button and use it there twice (the left button). With the
# fix the debris casts nothing. Without it (the original, the same recording with its
# enhancements chunk naming skip-intro alone) the first use casts Light and the second is
# refused, "You are not yet ready to cast another spell"
3000 key enter         # Journey Onward
4500 key enter         # the first saved game
9000 move 245 93       # the scroll, the pack's first slot
9300 mdown 245 93 right
9600 move 200 85
9900 move 150 75
10200 move 110 65      # into the view: thrown at the wall, which breaks it
10500 mup 110 65 right
13000 key 1            # look down, twice
13800 key 1
16000 move 128 113     # the debris on the carpet: "You see a pile of debris"
16300 mdown 128 113 right
16500 mup 128 113 right
18000 move 128 113     # the debris, dragged into the pack's first slot
18300 mdown 128 113 right
18600 move 190 100
18900 move 245 93
19200 mup 245 93 right
21000 mdown 245 93 left    # used, twice
21200 mup 245 93 left
23000 mdown 245 93 left
23200 mup 245 93 left
25000 move 110 100
